  "locked": false,
  "title": "[AMD][BACKEND][GFX9] Support blocked/shared order mismatch for direct-to-LDS loads",
  "user": {
    "login": "AlexAUT",
    "id": 3915112,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM5MTUxMTI=",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3915112?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/AlexAUT",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexAUT/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "When the blocked and shared encodings have different orders, the srcToShared layout will have contig=1 and therefore smaller than the blocked encoding. In these cases CoalesceAsyncCopy either did not rewrite the blocked encoding, or rewrote it incorrectly, so the final layouts did not produce warp coalesced writes.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, the lowering wrongly rejected a valid combination (see the new lit test) because it always bailed out when the global pointer contiguity did not agree with the srcToShared contiguity. But when the srcToShared contiguity is smaller than the pointer contiguity, we have to split the load into multiple smaller ops. The lowering already supports this, so the check was simply too tight.",
